<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 2.2 pct in March - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 2.2 pct in March - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 3.10 billion zlotys, or 2.2 percent, in March to 141.51 billion after a 1.6 pct rise in February, preliminary central bank figures showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 4.1 percent in the January-March period against 6.1 percent in the same period of last year.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		    MARCH    FEBRUARY   MARCH 96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	    2.2	  1.6	   2.3</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		 141.51  138.41(138.34) 110.64</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)    25.00   24.58 (24.57)  21.13</p>
<p>  National currency		   116.51  113.83(113.77)  89.51</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		  24.59   23.45 (23.45)  20.64</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector  87.83   85.36 (85.29)  59.56</p>
<p>NOTE - revised figures in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
